diff --git a/docs/verification/batch-01-items-1-19.md b/docs/verification/batch-01-items-1-19.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..f9e2ba9\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/verification/batch-01-items-1-19.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@\n+# Batch 01 Verification \u0026 Release Ledger (Items 1–19)\n+\n+## 1. Migration, Provisioning, and Rollout Commands\n+\n+### D1 and Platform Migrations\n+Apply D1 platform migrations in order:\n+```bash\n+npx wrangler d1 migrations apply PLATFORM_DB --local\n+npx wrangler d1 migrations apply PLATFORM_DB --remote\n+```\n+Key schema guarantees in migrations:\n+- `0034_space_hierarchy.sql`: `spaces` table has `parent_space_id`, `depth`, `tenancy_mode`, `agency_shell`, `scenario_type`.\n+- `0073_project_scoped_automation.sql`: Enforces `project_id NOT NULL` across `scheduled_jobs`, `scheduled_job_runs`, and `triggers`.\n+- `0075_phase1_runtime_security.sql`: Durable connector aliases, single-use capability nonces, and virtual CLI registries.\n+\n+### Durable Object SQLite Migrations\n+SpaceDO runs versioned migrations `1` through `41` automatically on initial invocation (`applyMigrations` inside `ensureInit`):\n+- Migration v10: SpaceDO `spaces` hierarchy table (root + department depth \u003c\u003d 1) and `cross_space_grants`.\n+- Migration v23: `projects.visibility` (`public` vs `private`), `project_members` ACL, and `exclusive_mode`.\n+- Migration v39: `tasks` table with JSON dependency tracking for in-project multi-agent DAGs.\n+- Migration v40: `event_triggers` constrained strictly to active project containers.\n+- Migration v41: `projects.execution_ceiling` expanded to support Tier 6 containers.\n+\n+### Secret Management \u0026 Rotations\n+Ensure required edge secrets are configured:\n+```bash\n+npx wrangler secret put PLATFORM_SECRET\n+npx wrangler secret put NAELAO_AIG_TOKEN\n+```\n+Rollback posture:\n+D1 migrations use explicit table renames and backups (`scheduled_jobs_v73`, `event_triggers_v40`). If rolling back, swap names back or restore from D1 point-in-time recovery.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 2. Test, Typecheck, and Parity Verification\n+\n+Execute automated test verification:\n+```bash\n+pnpm --filter @naelao/agent-sdk test\n+pnpm test packages/agent-sdk/src/workflow-taxonomy.test.ts\n+pnpm --filter naelao-artifact test\n+pnpm --filter naelao-spaces test\n+pnpm --filter naelao-agents test\n+pnpm test workers/agents/src/script-engine/r2-workspace.test.ts\n+pnpm test workers/agents/src/script-engine/execution-ladder.test.ts\n+pnpm test workers/spaces/src/project-automation.test.ts\n+pnpm test workers/agents/container/artifact-fs.test.mjs\n+pnpm test workers/agents/src/do/ToolSandboxDO.test.ts\n+pnpm --filter naelao-agents test\n+pnpm typecheck\n+```\n+\n+### Security and Invariant Assertions\n+1. **Hierarchy Invariant:** Root space must have `depth: 0` and `parent_id: null`. Department must have `depth: 1` and `parent_id` pointing to an active Launchpad root. Second-generation children (`depth: 2`) are rejected with `max_depth_exceeded`.\n+2. **Inheritance \u0026 Air-Gapping:** Downward oversight allows parent company admins to view and manage sub-spaces. Upward access from department members to parent company ledgers is rejected with `403`. Sibling sub-spaces have zero visibility by default, requiring an active `cross_space_grants` record.\n+3. **Confidential Workstation Concealment:** Querying an unauthorized private project returns an identical `404 Not Found` as an absent ID, leaking neither existence nor metadata.\n+4. **Namespace Integrity:** Paths starting with `/.avos/` are excluded from Git-tracked collection and cannot cross-traverse into `/workspace/`.\n+5. **Zero-Copy Micro-Forks:** Branching from a commit creates an isolated mutable ref with cloned worktree entries in sub-10ms without altering `main`.\n+6. **Turn-by-Turn Auditability \u0026 Blame:** Every commit enforces structured metadata (`agent_role`, `user_goal`, `task_id`, `rationale`, `thread_id`, `tool_turn_id`). File blame retrieves full provenance.\n+7. **6-Tier Execution Ladder:** Compute routes to cheapest viable tier: Tier 1 (VFS), Tier 2 (Isolate/Pyodide), Tier 3 (Workflows), Tier 4 (Kitesurf), Tier 5 (Chromium), Tier 6 (Container).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 3. Item-by-Item Release Ledger (Items 1–19)\n+\n+| Item | Specification Focus | Status | Implementation Boundaries \u0026 Verification Notes |\n+| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n+| **1** | Enterprise Depth Hierarchy | IMPLEMENTED | `defineLaunchpadSpace`, `createSpaceRecord`, `createSubSpaceRow`. Prohibits depth \u003e 1. Tested in `space-hierarchy-policy.test.ts` \u0026 `launchpad-runtime.test.ts`. |\n+| **2** | Sub-Space Inheritance \u0026 Isolation Matrix | IMPLEMENTED | `authorizeHierarchy`, `canAccessSpace`, `checkCrossSpace`. Downward admin oversight permitted; upward \u0026 lateral sibling access blocked unless explicit grant exists. |\n+| **3** | Public vs. Private Project Access Control | IMPLEMENTED | `authorizeProject`, `SpaceDO.getProject`, `listProjects`. Unauthorized access returns fail-closed `404 Not Found`. Verified in test suite. |\n+| **4** | Project-Anchored Automation Architecture | IMPLEMENTED | `requireManageableAutomationProject`, D1 migration 0073, `SpaceDO.createEventTrigger` (migration v40). Root-level floating automations denied. |\n+| **5** | Cloudflare Artifacts Git-for-Agents Engine | IMPLEMENTED | `RepositoryDO` and `repository.ts`. Git object envelope hashing, content-addressed storage in R2, mutable refs in DO. Verified in `repository.test.ts`. |\n+| **6** | In-Memory Virtual POSIX Shell (`@cloudflare/computer`) | IMPLEMENTED | `r2-workspace.ts` (`virtualFsRead`, `virtualFsWrite`, `virtualFsGrep`, `executeVirtualShell`), wired directly into `execution-ladder.ts` for Tier 1 VFS. |\n+| **7** | Clean Namespace Separation (`/workspace/` vs `/.avos/`) | IMPLEMENTED | `normalizeWorkspacePath`, `isGitTracked`, `server.mjs`. `.avos` excluded from Git collection and traversal across boundaries rejected. |\n+| **8** | 6-Tier Cloudflare Execution Ladder | IMPLEMENTED | `ExecutionTier` 1..6, `routeRuntime`, `code-runner.ts`, `execution-ladder.ts`. Lowest capable tier selected; result returns actual tier and engine. |\n+| **9** | Invisible Runtime Hypervisor | IMPLEMENTED | `routeRuntime`, `ScriptToolSurface.run`. Hypervisor abstracts execution infrastructure from prompt tool interfaces. |\n+| **10** | `ArtifactFS` FUSE Driver with Lazy Hydration | IMPLEMENTED | `artifact-fs.mjs` and `artifact-fs.test.mjs`. Metadata-only tree hydration on mount; file contents fetched on `open()`; writes flushed before atomic commit. |\n+| **11** | 4-Dimension State Synchronization Engine | IMPLEMENTED | `WorkspaceStateCoordinator`, `ToolSandboxDO.fetch(\u0027/session/state\u0027)`. State updates check revisions; stale updates reject with `workspace_state_conflict`. |\n+| **12** | 95/5 Compute Arbitrage with 60s Micro-Sleep | IMPLEMENTED | `shouldStopContainer`, `ToolSandboxDO.alarm()`. Lease boundaries evaluated at 59,999ms vs 60,000ms. State persists across hibernation. |\n+| **13** | In-Isolate WebAssembly Python (Pyodide) | IMPLEMENTED | `routeRuntime` classifies `pythonImports`. Non-native runs in Tier 2; native imports (`torch`, `cv2`) route or auto-promote to Tier 6 container. |\n+| **14** | Tier 4 Cloudflare Kitesurf Agent Browser | IMPLEMENTED | `runBrowser` in `code-runner.ts`. Lightweight Kitesurf used by default; auto-elevates to Chromium for WebGL or visual snapshots with etc/passwd\")).toThrow(\"Path escapes ArtifactFS root\");\n+  });\n });\ndiff --git a/workers/agents/container/server.mjs b/workers/agents/container/server.mjs\nindex 45167ad..c8b00ba 100644\n--- a/workers/agents/container/server.mjs\n+++ b/workers/agents/container/server.mjs\n@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@ async function collectWorkspace() {\n     for (const entry of entries) {\n       if (count \u003e\u003d MAX_WORKSPACE_FILES) return;\n       const full \u003d join(dir, entry.name);\n+      if (entry.name \u003d\u003d\u003d \".avos\") continue;\n       if (entry.isDirectory()) {\n         await walk(full);\n       } else if (entry.isFile()) {\n@@ -93,6 +94,7 @@ async function listWorkspacePaths() {\n     for (const entry of entries) {\n       if (names.length \u003e\u003d MAX_WORKSPACE_FILES) return;\n       const full \u003d join(dir, entry.name);\n+      if (entry.name \u003d\u003d\u003d \".avos\") continue;\n       if (entry.isDirectory()) await walk(full);\n       else if (entry.isFile()) names.push(relative(WORKSPACE_DIR, full));\n     }\n@@ -165,11 +167,25 @@ async function execScript(name, code, args) {\n }\n \n const WORKSPACE_ROUTES \u003d new Set([\"/workspace/read\", \"/workspace/write\", \"/workspace/list\", \"/workspace/delete\"]);\n+const DISPLAY_ROUTES \u003d new Set([\"/display/capture\", \"/display/mouse\", \"/display/type\"]);\n \n createServer((req, res) \u003d\u003e {\n   const path \u003d req.url ?? \"\";\n   const isWorkspaceRoute \u003d [...WORKSPACE_ROUTES].some((r) \u003d\u003e path.endsWith(r));\n-  if (req.method !\u003d\u003d \"POST\" || (!path.endsWith(\"/build\") \u0026\u0026 !path.endsWith(\"/exec\") \u0026\u0026 !isWorkspaceRoute)) {\n+  const isDisplayRoute \u003d [...DISPLAY_ROUTES].some((r) \u003d\u003e path.endsWith(r));\n+  if (req.method !\u003d\u003d \"POST\" || (!path.endsWith(\"/build\") \u0026\u0026 !path.endsWith(\"/exec\") \u0026\u0026 !isWorkspaceRoute \u0026\u0026 !isDisplayRoute)) {\n     res.writeHead(404).end(JSON.stringify({ error: \"not_found\" }));\n     return;\n   }\n@@ -188,6 +204,26 @@ createServer((req, res) \u003d\u003e {\n         res.writeHead(200, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" }).end(JSON.stringify(result));\n         return;\n       }\n+      if (isDisplayRoute) {\n+        if (path.endsWith(\"/display/capture\")) {\n+          try {\n+            const { execFileSync } \u003d await import(\"node:child_process\");\n+            const frame \u003d execFileSync(\"scrot\", [\"-z\", \"-o\", \"-\"], { env: { ...process.env, DI